Sun= 200+50*SIN(2*3.14159*Time/12)
	~	Dmnl
	~	Exogenous driver. Seasonal cycle stands in for Sun's varying intensity.
	|

Water Temperature= 10+0.05*Sun
	~	Celsius
	~	Driven by Sun, as in the diagram (Sun -> Water Temperature).
	|

Evaporation= 0.01*Water Temperature
	~	m/Month
	~	Driven by Water Temperature. No downstream link, matching the diagram (Water Temperature -> Evaporation, a dead end).
	|

External Migratory Animals= 2
	~	Ton/Month
	~	Exogenous input. Diagram label: 'Animals - external/migratory' (-> Plants).
	|

Agriculture with Fertilizer= 5
	~	Ton/Month
	~	Exogenous input (-> Nutrient Levels).
	|

Pollution Microplastic= 0.3
	~	Dmnl
	~	Exogenous input, 0 (none) to 1 (severe). Diagram label: 'Pollution / Microplastic' (-> Food).
	|

Food= 0.1*(1-Pollution Microplastic)
	~	1/Month
	~	Diagram label: 'Food (over-/under-fishing)'. Higher pollution is assumed to suppress fishing activity, lowering Food.
	|

O2 Levels= INTEG (
	0.05*Plants-0.01*(Water Temperature-20)-0.08*O2 Levels,
		8)
	~	Ton
	~	O2 Levels. Produced by Plants, reduced by warmer Water Temperature, with a natural return toward equilibrium.
	|

Plants= INTEG (
	0.05*Nutrient Levels+External Migratory Animals+0.01*O2 Levels-0.02*Fish Stock-0.05*Plants,
		50)
	~	Ton
	~	Plants. Fed by Nutrient Levels, O2 Levels and External Migratory Animals; grazed by Fish Stock; a self-decay term closes the loop back to Nutrient Levels.
	|

Nutrient Levels= INTEG (
	Agriculture with Fertilizer+0.02*Plants+0.01*Fish Stock-0.08*Nutrient Levels,
		20)
	~	Ton
	~	Nutrient Levels. Fed by Agriculture, by Plants decaying, and by Fish Stock waste; consumed as it supports Plants.
	|

Fish Stock= INTEG (
	0.02*Plants+0.01*O2 Levels-Food*Fish Stock-0.02*Fish Stock,
		40)
	~	Ton
	~	Fish Stock -- the headline output. Supported by Plants and O2 Levels; removed by Food (fishing pressure) and natural mortality.
	|

FINAL TIME  = 240
	~	Month
	~	The final time for the simulation (20 years).
	|

INITIAL TIME  = 0
	~	Month
	~	The initial time for the simulation.
	|

SAVEPER  = 
        TIME STEP
	~	Month [0,?]
	~	The frequency with which output is stored.
	|

TIME STEP  = 1
	~	Month [0,?]
	~	The time step for the simulation.
	|

